@startuml

title Proposed simpler architecture — services, code modules, storage and messaging
top to bottom direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam nodesep 20
skinparam ranksep 30
skinparam wrapWidth 320
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam ArrowColor #475569
skinparam componentBackgroundColor #EFF6FF
skinparam databaseBackgroundColor #F1F5F9
skinparam queueBackgroundColor #FEF3C7

actor "Passenger\nWeb / mobile client" as client
component "API Gateway\nTLS, routing, authentication checks\nNo ticket business logic" as gateway #E2E8F0
cloud "Identity provider\nExternal OIDC system" as identity
cloud "Payment provider\nExternal system" as provider
cloud "Email / SMS provider\nExternal system" as mail


component "Schedule service\n----\nCode modules inside this process:\napi\nschedule — trips, routes, stations\njourney_search — from / to / date\nrolling_stock — trains, seats\npersistence + outbox publisher" as schedule
component "Sales service\n----\nCode modules inside this process:\napi\nbooking — orders, fares, tickets\ninventory — segments, holds, allocations\npassengers — profiles, documents\ncheckout — payment saga, timers\npersistence + inbox / outbox" as sales
component "Payment service\n----\nCode modules inside this process:\napi + signed webhook handler\npayments + refunds\nprovider_adapter + reconciliation\npersistence + outbox publisher" as payment
component "Notification service\nBackground worker + internal status API\n----\nCode modules:\nevent_consumer + templates\nemail_adapter + sms_adapter\nretry_scheduler + delivery_log\npersistence + inbox / outbox" as notification
component "Audit service\nBackground worker + restricted history API\n----\nCode modules:\nevent_consumer\nhistory_writer + history_query\npersistence + deduplication" as audit

database "schedule_db\nPostgreSQL\n----\ntrips, stops, routes, trains, seats\nsearch indexes / SQL read model\noutbox" as sdb
database "sales_db\nPostgreSQL\n----\nbookings, tickets, fares\nseat_segments, holds, allocations\npassenger_profiles, documents\nsaga_state, inbox, outbox" as bdb
database "payment_db\nPostgreSQL\n----\npayments, attempts, refunds\nprovider_events, outbox" as pdb
database "notification_db\nPostgreSQL\n----\njobs, attempts, templates\ninbox, outbox" as ndb
database "audit_db\nSeparate PostgreSQL history store\n----\nappend-only business events\nunique event_id" as adb
queue "Kafka\nOne logical broker cluster\n----\nschedule.events\nsales.events\npayment.events\nnotification.events\nConsumer-specific retry / failure handling" as kafka

client --> gateway : HTTPS
client --> provider : hosted checkout
gateway --> identity : OIDC / JWKS
gateway --> schedule : journey search
gateway --> sales : booking / profiles
gateway --> payment : webhook
provider --> gateway : signed webhook
sales --> schedule : validate trip
sales --> payment : payment / refund
payment --> provider : payment API
notification --> mail : HTTPS: send
schedule --> sdb : SQL
sales --> bdb : SQL
payment --> pdb : SQL
notification --> ndb : SQL
audit --> adb : SQL
schedule -[#B45309,dashed]-> kafka : publish
sales -[#B45309,dashed]-> kafka : publish
payment -[#B45309,dashed]-> kafka : publish
notification -[#B45309,dashed]-> kafka : publish
kafka -[#B45309,dashed]-> sales : schedule + payments
kafka -[#B45309,dashed]-> notification : tickets
kafka -[#B45309,dashed]-> audit : all events

legend bottom
Blue boxes = service deployments; the listed code modules are NOT separate processes.
Solid arrows = requests / SQL. Dashed orange arrows = asynchronous event flow.
Notification receives the required delivery contact in a restricted event payload.
Audit persists a redacted subset of events; no passenger document numbers in general event streams.
Private databases may share a PostgreSQL cluster in a lab; they do not share application tables.
Production replicas, backups and failure domains are not expanded in this logical view.
DevOps operates deployments, CI/CD, secrets, metrics, logs and tracing across all services.
Not included by default: separate Search service, OpenSearch, Redis, Kubernetes.
endlegend
@enduml



